WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:07.260
Christian Page knows what it means to lead
an insecure, unstructured life.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.580
He spent over three years hanging out with
this group of homeless people at the Place

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.110
Sainte Marthe in Paris.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.180
He used to have a well-paid job as a sommelier.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.739
But after his wife left him, he started drinking.

00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:24.060
And when he could no longer pay the rent he
ended up on the streets

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:33.559
"This is one of the places I slept in.

00:00:33.559 --> 00:00:39.260
But a few weeks later, they installed these
typically anti-homeless barriers.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:46.450
They're placed deliberately so no-one can
doss down here."

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.480
The residents are a bit ashamed of the barriers
but they are glad there are no homeless people

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.650
sleeping here.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:58.220
"They didn't bother anyone, but it was dirty.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.060
I'm not sure what to think.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.440
It doesn't look nice but at least perhaps
now they are living in better conditions than

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.299
this entrance where there was lots of garbage."

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.990
Anti-homeless barriers have popped up all
over Paris.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:16.270
After Christian tweeted angrily about barriers
that had been set up here, where people sometimes

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:22.369
lie because there is warm air from the metro,
he was able to make a change.

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:28.640
"The city of Paris had put in iron rods to
prevent access.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:32.700
You can still see the traces.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:39.979
They would have stopped people from being
able to sleep there in winter when it's cold.

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:49.860
I posted it on twitter and the next day the
city authorities removed the iron rods."

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.450
Christian posted his first tweet three years
ago - after his possessions were soaked by

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.959
street cleaners.

00:01:55.959 --> 00:02:01.090
It was winter and he wrote: "This is how the
homeless are treated in Paris."

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:09.030
Within a few months, he had over 30,000 followers.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.830
"I'd tweet in the morning to say hello to
the planet and at night to talk about what

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:19.650
was going on the street.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:24.610
I'd take a picture of my sleeping bag and
say "good night guys", then go to bed.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:29.010
And people would answer, good night, see you
tomorrow.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.010
I thought it was cool."

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:37.550
With his tweets, Christian was able to draw
attention to the main problems homeless people

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.860
face in Paris - something his friends appreciate.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.610
His friend Lionel doesn't have a phone.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:49.880
To get one, he'd have to overcome too many
hurdles that appear insurmountable to him.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:55.030
"I don't even have a bank account.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:59.570
I do but it's blocked.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:04.340
My papers are at the lost and found office
and I have to pay 11 euros to get them back

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:09.310
and on top of that they'll ask me for my papers.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.180
But i don't have them."

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.340
People who live on the streets often feel
like pariahs.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.910
But Christian Page has given them a voice.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.500
And his activism has spread beyond Paris.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:26.030
People send him pictures of barricades from
elsewhere in France.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:30.470
This one's from Narbonne in the south.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:39.120
"It's true that the social media have a certain
power that can be negative for big brands.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:47.620
We'll see in the next few days that Yves Rocher
will certainly get rid of those barriers."

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.830
Christian is glad that his tweets can change
things for the better.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.300
His own situation has now changed for the
better, too.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:58.390
He has found accommodation, at least for the
time being, with a Christian aid organization.

